            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Fast Feedback Rule",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Push each check to the ==lowest level== that can still catch the bug",
                "Logic bug: unit test, not a browser run",
                "Wiring or schema bug: integration test",
                "Only critical user flows earn an E2E test"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Shapes and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Shape",
                "Emphasis",
                "Verdict"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Pyramid",
                  "Unit base",
                  "{green:Healthy}"
                ],
                [
                  "Ice-cream cone",
                  "Manual or E2E, few units",
                  "{red:Slow, brittle}"
                ],
                [
                  "Trophy",
                  "Static analysis base, integration",
                  "Units are thin glue"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Ice-cream cone",
              "text": "Mostly manual or ==E2E== tests with few unit tests gives a **slow, brittle** suite."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not test everything E2E?** Slow, costly, flaky, hard to debug",
                "**When pick the trophy?** When units are thin glue code"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Unit vs Integration vs End-to-End",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unit vs Integration vs End-to-End",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Levels",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Unit}: one function or class, dependencies swapped for ==mocks, stubs or fakes==",
                "Runs in **milliseconds**, no network or disk",
                "{orange:Integration}: several ==real components== together, e.g. service + real database",
                "Catches **wiring, schema and config** bugs",
                "{purple:E2E}: whole system through the UI or public API, like a user",
                "Playwright or Cypress on a login-to-checkout flow"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Unit",
                "Integration",
                "E2E"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "{green:fast}",
                  "{orange:medium}",
                  "{red:slow}"
                ],
                [
                  "Failures",
                  "**precise**",
                  "realistic",
                  "most realistic"
                ],
                [
                  "How many",
                  "most",
                  "some",
                  "==fewest=="
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Login",
