    {
      "title": "Code Coverage",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Code Coverage",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What It Measures",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Coverage== = share of code **executed** by tests",
                "{blue:Line}: lines run. {purple:Function}: functions called",
                "{green:Branch}: every if/else path, so ==stricter== than line",
                "One test can hit a line yet skip the other branch"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def fee(n):",
                "    if n > 100:",
                "        n -= 10",
                "    return n",
                "assert fee(200) == 190"
              ],
              "note": "100% line, but the False branch never ran"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Running It",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Stack",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Python",
                  "`pytest --cov=src --cov-branch`"
                ],
                [
                  "JavaScript",
                  "`jest --coverage`"
                ],
                [
                  "Go",
                  "`go test -cover`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Reports come out as ==lcov== or **HTML**",
                "Use the report to find untested paths"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Limits and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "100% does not prove correctness: executed is not ==asserted==",
                "Assertion-free tests only chase the number",
                "Check test strength with ==mutation testing==: Stryker, mutmut"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Floor on new code",
              "text": "Use coverage to find gaps, not as a goal. Enforce a ==floor on new code==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Flaky Tests and Quality Gates",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Flaky Tests and Quality Gates",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Flaky Tests",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Flaky test== = passes and fails on the **same code**",
                "Eroded trust: people stop believing red builds"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cause",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Timing, sleeps",
                  "Wait on a ==condition==, not a sleep"
                ],
                [
                  "Shared state, test order",
                  "Isolate state per test"
                ],
                [
                  "Unseeded randomness, real clock",
                  "Inject fixed seeds and clocks"
                ],
                [
                  "Real network",
                  "Mock external services"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Quarantine, don't retry",
              "text": "Tag the test and track a ==ticket== at once. **Auto-retry** hides the flake."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Quality Gates",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Quality gate== = automated pass/fail in CI that **blocks merge**",
                "Tests green, lint clean, type check",
                "Coverage on new code at or above threshold",
                "No critical vulnerabilities"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Lint",
                    "sub": "seconds",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Types",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Tests",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Coverage",
                    "sub": "new code",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Scan",
                    "sub": "vulns",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Slow or noisy gates get ==bypassed==",
                "Run fast checks first; require them on protected branches",
                "Gate **new code**, not the whole legacy base"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not auto-retry flaky tests?** It hides the cause and erodes trust.",
                "**What does a gate block?** Merge, unless tests, lint, types, coverage pass."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
